1. Array Creation
let arr1 = [1, 2, 3];
let arr2 = new Array(1, 2, 3);
let arr3 = Array.of(1, 2, 3);
let arr4 = Array.from('hello'); // ['h','e','l','l','o']

2. Adding / Removing Elements
Method	Description	Example
push()	Add element at end	arr.push(4)
pop()	Remove last element	arr.pop()
unshift()	Add element at start	arr.unshift(0)
shift()	Remove first element	arr.shift()
splice()	Add/remove at index	arr.splice(1, 0, 5) adds 5 at index 1
concat()	Merge arrays	[1,2].concat([3,4]) → [1,2,3,4]
3. Access / Search
Method	Description	Example
indexOf()	First occurrence index	[1,2,3].indexOf(2) → 1
lastIndexOf()	Last occurrence index	[1,2,2].lastIndexOf(2) → 2
includes()	Check existence	[1,2,3].includes(2) → true
find()	Find first matching element	[1,2,3].find(x => x>1) → 2
findIndex()	Index of first match	[1,2,3].findIndex(x => x>1) → 1
at()	Access by index, supports negative	[1,2,3].at(-1) → 3
4. Iteration / Transformation
Method	Description	Example
forEach()	Loop through each element	arr.forEach(x => console.log(x))
map()	Transform array	[1,2,3].map(x => x*2) → [2,4,6]
filter()	Filter elements	[1,2,3].filter(x => x>1) → [2,3]
reduce()	Reduce to single value	[1,2,3].reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) → 6
reduceRight()	Reduce from right	[1,2,3].reduceRight((a,b)=>a-b) → 0
some()	At least one matches	[1,2,3].some(x=>x>2) → true
every()	All match	[1,2,3].every(x=>x>0) → true
5. Sorting / Reversing
Method	Description	Example
sort()	Sort array	[3,1,2].sort() → [1,2,3]
reverse()	Reverse array	[1,2,3].reverse() → [3,2,1]
6. Join / Split
Method	Description	Example
join()	Convert to string	[1,2,3].join('-') → "1-2-3"
toString()	Convert to string	[1,2,3].toString() → "1,2,3"
7. Copy / Slice
Method	Description	Example
slice()	Copy part of array	[1,2,3,4].slice(1,3) → [2,3]
copyWithin()	Copy within array	[1,2,3,4].copyWithin(0,2) → [3,4,3,4]
fill()	Fill with value	[1,2,3].fill(0) → [0,0,0]
8. Array Checking / Conversion
Method	Description	Example
Array.isArray()	Check if array	Array.isArray([1,2]) → true
flat()	Flatten nested array	[1,[2,3]].flat() → [1,2,3]
flatMap()	Map then flatten	[1,2].flatMap(x=>[x,x*2]) → [1,2,2,4]
9. Other Useful Methods
Method	Description	Example
entries()	Iterator of [index,value]	for(const [i,v] of arr.entries())
keys()	Iterator of indices	for(const k of arr.keys())
values()	Iterator of values	for(const v of arr.values())
findLast()	Last element matching	[1,2,3,4].findLast(x=>x<4) → 3
findLastIndex()	Last index matching	[1,2,3,4].findLastIndex(x=>x<4) → 2
